a-not-yet-naming-starting-qb-game-vs-purdue","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama's Kalen DeBoer expects QB Keelon Russell to be 'full go' vs. Auburn","description":"Alabama coach Kalen DeBoer said Monday that he expects QB Keelon Russell, who is working his way back from an ankle injury, to be \"full go\" for rivalry week against Auburn.","published":"2026-11-23T18:13:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50574915/alabama-deboer-expects-qb-russell-full-go-auburn","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5150710/jermaine-mathews-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jermaine_Mathews_Jr."},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jermaine Mathews Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jermaine_Mathews_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:19Z","intro":"Jermaine Mathews Jr. (born March 28, 2005) is an American college football cornerback for the Ohio State Buckeyes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Mathews Jr. attended Winton Woods High School in Forest Park, Ohio. As a senior, he had 51 tackles, six interceptions with three of them returned for a touchdown. He committed to Ohio State University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Mathews Jr. earned playing time as a true freshman at Ohio State in 2023. He was named a freshman All-American."}]}}